      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "During the digestive procedure, pancreatic lipase is known as the main enzyme in vivo for digestion and absorption of dietary fat, consisting of pancreatic triglyceride lipase, pancreatic lipase related proteins 1 and 2, bile salt - stimulated Lipase and phospholipase A2. The changes of the development pattern of pancreatic lipase have confirmed associations with metabolic diseases such as obesity, not only because age is connected with the development of pancreatic lipase, but also pancreatic lipase itself is regulated by the dietary structure and endocrine hormone."},
